From 2f191c1966e140a45e96652ecc7924725670c785 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Murphy <christian.murphy.42@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:45:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Reject an empty segment in a mount root

A MountPoint could start with an empty segment, and every link under it then started with //, which a browser reads as another host. MountPoint now refuses the segments that unlinkable names, as a String capture does. MountPoint.ofSegs? returns none for an empty segment, and a literal root with one fails to compile. unlinkable moves next to dotSegment in Pattern.lean.

This changes behaviour for code that builds such a root, which now gets none or a compile error.

Signed-off-by: Christian Murphy <christian.murphy.42@gmail.com>
